.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt PHP2SHELL-REMEDIATE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm php2shell-remediate
.Nd classify a PHP point release against the php2shell advisory and report remediation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm classify
.Ar version-string
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
determines whether an observed PHP point release is exposed to
CVE-2026-109618 / CVE-2026-109619
.Pq Dq php2shell ,
the deserialization flaw disclosed on 2026-10-21, and reports what
remediation the result implies.
.Pp
The decision core is pure: it performs no network access, no process execution,
and carries no payload. It answers only the question
.Dq is this version exposed, and what closes it .
.Pp
The project additionally ships a benevolent proof-of-concept (the
.Pa examples/benevolent-poc
directory) whose only action is to disable the vulnerable feature on a system
you own \(em a way to test and verify exposure by securing it, before a patch is
applied. It is BSD-2-Clause licensed like the rest of the project, and is not
part of this command.
.Pp
The single subcommand,
.Cm classify ,
takes one
.Ar version-string .
That string may be a bare version
.Pq Li 8.2.35 ,
an
.Li X-Powered-By
header value
.Pq Li PHP/8.2.35 ,
or a distribution build string carrying a suffix after the patch level
.Pq Li 8.1.29-1+deb.sury.org+1 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
Patched: the version is at or above the fixed point release on its branch.
.It 1
Not clear of the advisory: exposed, an end-of-life branch, or a branch the
advisory does not name.
.It 2
Bad input: the argument could not be parsed as a three-component version.
.El
.Sh FIXED VERSIONS
The 2026-10-21 advisory names these fixed point releases:
.Bl -column "8.5" "8.5.12" -offset indent
.It Sy Branch Ta Sy Fixed in
.It 8.5 Ta 8.5.12
.It 8.4 Ta 8.4.27
.It 8.3 Ta 8.3.36
.It 8.2 Ta 8.2.35
.El
.Pp
PHP 7.4, 8.0 and 8.1 are end-of-life and received source-only backports rather
than a vendor binary point release;
.Nm
reports those separately rather than naming a fixed version it cannot vouch
for. A branch the advisory does not name is reported as
.Li UNKNOWN-BRANCH
and is never guessed into patched or exposed.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ php2shell-remediate classify PHP/8.4.26
EXPOSED 8.4.26 \(em fixed in 8.4.27

$ php2shell-remediate classify 8.4.27
PATCHED 8.4.27

$ php2shell-remediate classify 8.1.29
EOL-BRANCH 8.1.29 \(em source-only backport, no vendor point release
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
The project MANUAL.md for the library API
.Pq Fn classify_exposure , Fn plan_remediation , Fn interpret_probe
and the remediation workflow.
.Sh STANDARDS
Version strings are matched against the advisory table only; no inference is
made beyond the branches the advisory names.
